# Imports and lib modules

## Use the `@/` alias

```typescript
import { ProductGrid } from "@/components/shop";
import { pageMetadata } from "@/lib/seo";
import { useAuth } from "@/contexts/AuthContext";
```

Never use long relative paths across feature boundaries (`../../../components/...`).

## Lib module map

| Module | Import from | Responsibility |
|--------|-------------|----------------|
| HTTP / API | `@/lib/api` | `getApiUrl`, `getAuthHeaders`, `apiFetch` |
| Auth | `@/lib/auth` | tokens, session, Google sign-in |
| Catalog | `@/lib/catalog` | grouped products, filters, nav catalog, swatches |
| Products | `@/lib/products` | images, product page loader, reviews API |
| SEO | `@/lib/seo` | metadata helpers, JSON-LD builders |
| Drive | `@/lib/drive` | Google Drive file browser |

## Naming collision in `@/lib/catalog`

- `categoriasForClase` from `@/lib/catalog` → shop filter meta (admin products list, navbar)
- Vitrina/item characteristics version → import from `@/lib/catalog/itemCharacteristics`

## Keep imports at the public boundary

Import from barrel `index.ts` files, not deep internal paths, unless accessing a module intentionally not re-exported (e.g. `itemCharacteristics` above).
